/*! \page page_res AnCH configuration library documentation
 *
 * \tableofcontents
 *
 * \section res_intro_seq Introduction
 *
 * AnCh configuration library aims to provide facilities to handle configuration files.
 *
 * \section res_req_sec Prerequisites
 *
 * - \ref page_ini "anch-ini": this is the default configuration file parser (it will be register with extensions \c ini , \c conf , \c cnf and \c properties files)
 *
 * \section res_install_sec Installation
 *
 * CMake target \c anch::conf:
 * \code{.cmake}
find_package(Anch REQUIRED)
target_link_libraries(my-app PRIVATE anch::conf)
\endcode
 * See \ref install_sec "installation".
 *
 * \section res_concept_sec Conception
 *
 * Configuration is loaded once with \ref anch::conf::Configuration::loader "Configuration::loader()" and
 * read with \ref anch::conf::Configuration::inst "Configuration::inst()". Values are read with dotted paths
 * (\c section.subsection.key ).
 *
 * \subsection res_cascade_sec Cascade
 *
 * \code{.ini}
# application.ini
anch::conf.includes=database,security
anch::conf.default-profiles=dev

[server]
host=${env=HOST|localhost}
url=http://${conf=server.host}:${conf=server.port}/
\endcode
 *
 * Loading order (later files override previous values): \c application , included files
 * (\c database , \c security ), then for each active profile \c application-\<profile\> and
 * \c \<include\>-\<profile\> when they exist. Active profiles are given to \c profiles() , or set in
 * \c ANCH_PROFILES environment variable, or \c anch::conf.default-profiles .
 *
 * \subsection res_placeholders_sec Placeholders
 *
 * <tt>${alternative|alternative|...}</tt>: an alternative is <tt>resolver=argument</tt> (\c env , \c conf
 * or registered resolvers) or a default value; the first alternative which resolves is used.
 * Resolution is event driven (a resolved value completes the values which reference it) and has a
 * watchdog: cycles and too long resolution chains are errors (\c CYCLE ). Resolved values are literal.
 *
 * \section res_example_sec Example
 *
 * \code{.cpp}
#include "conf/configuration.hpp"

const anch::conf::Configuration& conf = anch::conf::Configuration::loader()
  .name("application")
  .folders({"/etc/myapp", "."})
  .load();
std::optional<std::string> url = conf.value("server.url");
\endcode
 */
